// The kind control beside `shadow_enum_over_generic_struct`: a user STRUCT of
// the same name. It DOES remove the prelude declaration - the drop is matched by
// kind - so the arity really is 0 and this program really is wrong.
//
// Keeping it is what stops the fix from being described as "the arity check now
// prefers the prelude". It prefers whatever RESOLUTION bound, and here that is
// the user's struct. Green on both sides before and after; a fix that turned this
// into an acceptance would have traded one direction for the other.
struct Vec { a: int }

fn takes(v: *const Vec<int>) { println(1); }

fn main() { println(1); }
